Step 3 (`annotate` guardrails) leaves the case where the source has some accepted guardrail headings and lacks others undecided. It says the model supplies bodies "When it has no accepted heading, the existing single `annotate` call also returns the missing guardrail bodies". The plan's Architecture table says "otherwise the existing `annotate` call writes them". Step 2's helper decides copy-or-`_(TODO)_` per heading, but the model fallback reads as whole-source. A source plan with `## Scope guardrails` and nothing else has three readings:
  - copy the one heading and ask the model for the other two;
  - copy the one heading and write `_(TODO)_` for the other two;
  - treat the source as "has a heading", or ask the model for all three and overwrite the inherited one.

  The written seed and the printed review list ("model-written or inherited") differ across these readings, and no sentence in the plan picks one.
